So on my server, `/` 404s. Because with appType 'custom', vite middlewares don't serve index.html at `/`. I must serve it myself. Fix: in the server, for non-/api GET requests, serve index.html via vite.transformIndexHtml, or simply read index.html and serve with transform. Simplest:

```ts
if (req.method === 'GET' && (path === '/' || path === '/index.html')) {
  const html = await vite.transformIndexHtml('/', readFileSync('index.html', 'utf8'));
  res.writeHead(200, {'content-type': 'text/html'});
  res.end(html);
  return;
}
```

transformIndexHtml needs the URL. Then vite.middlewares for everything else.

